A carve keeps the bits it names rather than those of them its source may signal,
so a carve of a client's capability widens it to bits the client was never given;
a node is derived from its parent, a notification's capability with no more bits.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-smp2 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: slot is not derived from its parent

diff --git a/kernel/syscall.c b/kernel/syscall.c
--- a/kernel/syscall.c
+++ b/kernel/syscall.c
@@ -505,7 +505,7 @@ static int op_notification(struct thread *t, uint32_t slot, const struct cap *ca
     case OP_NOTIFY_CARVE: {
         /* Fewer bits, as a carve of a frame is less memory: a table operation, below the invoked capability. */
         struct cap sub = *cap;
-        sub.b &= arg[1];
+        sub.b = arg[1];
         if (sub.b == 0) {
             return KERR_INVALID_ARG;
         }
